## 0. PROJECT SCALE & DOCUMENT MODEL
Classify the project first, then apply the matching doc set. Re-evaluate when triggers below are hit.

| Scale | Signals | Required docs |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **S (small)** | Single process, ≤1 dev, script/demo, no DB migration | `.docs/SPEC.md` |
| **M (medium)** | Multi-module / has API layer / DB / external integrations / 2+ devs | `.docs/SPEC.md`; `.docs/API.md` only when explicitly requested or already established |
| **L (large)** | 2+ independently deployable services / production environment / multiple teams | `.docs/SPEC.md`; any additional document requires explicit user request |
| **Optional** | Product rationale needed / history matters | `.docs/PRD.md`, `.docs/DEV_LOG.md` |

**Upgrade triggers (S → M): expand the design depth inside `.docs/SPEC.md` when ANY occurs**:
- A backend API / multi-service split is introduced.
- A database or a migration-bearing store is added or swapped.
- A second developer joins, or cross-module boundaries appear.
- Architecture can no longer be stated in one sentence.

**Upgrade triggers (M → L): expand the design depth inside `.docs/SPEC.md` when ANY occurs**:
- A second independently deployable service appears.
- A production/staging environment or CI/CD pipeline is established.
- A second team or ownership boundary appears.

**L-scale specifics**:
- Significant decisions use an ADR-style subsection inside `.docs/SPEC.md`（context, options, decision, consequences）。
- Environments, build/deploy, config/secrets sourcing, rollback and observability remain dedicated sections inside `.docs/SPEC.md`。
- Sub-directory execution rules may exist only when the user explicitly requests them；they do not own technical design。

**Target Workspace Layout**:
```text
project/
├── .cursor/
│   ├── agents/         # Agent personas (*.md at this root)
│   └── rules/          # Project rules (*.mdc)
├── .docs/
│   ├── PRD.md          # Optional: product intent, users, scope and acceptance
│   ├── SPEC.md         # Required: all technical design and development DAG
│   ├── API.md          # Optional: only when explicitly requested or already established
│   ├── memory.md       # Optional user-controlled current context
│   └── DEV_LOG.md      # Optional append-only history
└── <repository-defined source roots>
```

**Doc Handling Rules**:
- If `.docs/SPEC.md` is missing: list it in chat; do not create until the user authorizes the technical-design task.
- All scales keep architecture, decisions, deployment, security, observability, tests and DAG inside `.docs/SPEC.md`; do not propose separate technical-design documents unless the user explicitly asks.
- `.docs/SPEC.md` / established `.docs/API.md`: draft changes first when scope is not already confirmed; persist only per #0.1.
- Never mix AI config into `src/` or the repo root unless the framework requires it.

