## 0.1 .docs I/O (HARD CONSTRAINT · user-triggered only)
Paths: project contracts and progress files all live under `.docs/`: `PRD.md` / `SPEC.md` / `API.md` / `memory.md` / `DEV_LOG.md`.  
**Prohibited**: Auto-reading, auto-creating, or auto-updating documents on session start / role switch / DoD / feature completion / context compression / scale upgrade.

| File | Read Authority | Write Authority |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `memory.md` + `DEV_LOG.md` | Write-intent turn may read both to sync; otherwise only when user `@`s that file | Unified intent **「更新」**（亦认：「更新进度」/「更新进程」/「进度更新」/「同步进度」/「更新日志」/「日志更新」/「记录里程碑」）→ **同轮同时**：重写 `memory.md`（当前态）+ 向 `DEV_LOG.md` 追加一条已确认里程碑 → 输出 `[System: memory.md 已同步]` 与 `[System: DEV_LOG.md 已同步]` → **再**按 §5.2 输出 `下一步：【Pass|No Pass】------> …` |
| Project contracts (`.docs/PRD.md` / `.docs/SPEC.md` / established `.docs/API.md`) | Read when the user asks for project/design work or explicitly mentions the file | Write only when the user requests creation, optimization or modification |

**Content constraints**:
- Write only confirmed, executed content; keep undecided discussions in chat.
- On「更新」intent: both `.docs/memory.md` and `.docs/DEV_LOG.md` may be written in the same turn; other `.docs/` files still require an explicit create/modify/optimize request or direct file reference as defined above.
- When not authorized: full drafts may appear in chat, but write tools must NOT touch `.docs/`.
- If `memory.md` or `DEV_LOG.md` does not exist: create on「更新」intent.

